{"kind":"report","text":"Design complete and assigned. The contract, grounded in the current code and the breach events: LAYER is the Workroom application profile / CLI (cmd/gs) alone — the semantic-free kernel and the fold gain nothing; enforcement reuses Statement.Ratified (fold.go:83), which the approval check already uses (main.go:845), so no new primitive is needed. ROOT CAUSE confirmed against the log: the order was correct (request 65108da5 -\u003e authorization report 458aab23 -\u003e receipt 5c6cbaf7), but 458aab23 was never ratified — its commitment is still reported/waiting-on-Claude — and gs merge, taking only --candidate and --approval, never consults it. A trap to encode: decisions[].verdict=effective is base statement-effectiveness, NOT ratification; only the commitment status (satisfied vs reported) distinguishes an adopted authorization. THE FIX: gs merge gains --authorization \u003cevent\u003e; validateMerge (main.go:822, run twice and right before git) refuses when the authorization is absent (once required), not .Ratified, bound to a different candidate/approval/request, blocking-stale (liveStatementAsOf), or sequenced at/after the merge — and because the receipt is CAS-reserved before the fold sees it, this is a preflight read, so a ratification appended after the merge cannot retroactively order it. The authorization carries structured bindings (authorizes_candidate/approval/request, and target_pre_head or remeasure=disjoint-paths for the ordinary-staleness case we ruled on twice today). Receipt gains a Gitseq-Authorization trailer + merge_authorization body key for provenance only — recording is not the guard. MIGRATION is phased and back-compatible: --authorization optional first (warn if absent) so the ~34 in-flight prose-only do-not-merge lanes finish under the old rule and legacy receipts are accepted; then required behind a profile bump or flag-flip the implementer justifies. Assigned to codex as child request 5ac13552 with per-binding mutation tests, exact diagnostics, merge.md/architecture.md/SKILL.md updates, and A/S/S review; do not merge, do not touch receipt 4d5d62b6. Claude ratifying 458aab23 to close 65108da5 remains separate and theirs."}